          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5.1 How Can We Classify Mixtures?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.116,
            0.187,
            0.153
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 3,
              "bbox": [
                0.112,
                0.116,
                0.187,
                0.153
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_1_image_3.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.108,
            0.114,
            0.641,
            0.267
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Grade 8 You have learnt that a mixture of sugar and CuriosityChapter 9 water has a uniform composition throughout. A well-stirred mixture of sugar and water is equally sweet in the first and the last sip. Such a mixture is called a "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "homogeneous mixture",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (Fig. 5.1) or a "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "solution",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". Other examples of homogeneous mixtures are vinegar (acetic acid in water), aerated drinks like soda (carbon dioxide in water), etc. A solution always remains homogeneous."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.685,
            0.089,
            0.907,
            0.261
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 5,
              "bbox": [
                0.685,
                0.089,
                0.907,
                0.261
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_1_image_5.jpg",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "image_caption",
              "index": 7,
              "bbox": [
                0.683,
                0.268,
                0.908,
                0.284
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 5.1: Homogeneous mixture"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.107,
            0.269,
            0.641,
            0.372
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "On the other hand, a stirred mixture of sand and water is not uniform. The sand particles are easily visible in the water and settle with time. Such a mixture is called a "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "heterogeneous mixture",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (Fig. 5.2). Is the mixture of oil and water homogeneous or heterogeneous? Can you think of some other heterogeneous mixtures?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.109,
            0.38,
            0.606,
            0.399
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Activity 5.1: Let us experiment — Group activity"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.108,
            0.401,
            0.64,
            0.454
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Divide the class into three groups — A, B and C. Each group prepares a mixture in a colourless, transparent glass tumbler or a 100 mL beaker by following these steps:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.681,
            0.292,
            0.905,
            0.46
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 10,
              "bbox": [
                0.681,
                0.292,
                0.905,
                0.46
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_1_image_10.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.121,
            0.455,
            0.641,
            0.506
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. Group A: Add one spatula of common salt to 50 mL of water in a beaker and stir it well. Label it A."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.121,
            0.509,
            0.47,
            0.561
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. Group B: Add one spatula of chalk powder to 50 mL of water in a beaker and stir it well. Label it B."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.122,
            0.564,
            0.471,
            0.615
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. Group C: Add a few drops of milk to 50 mL of water in a beaker and stir it well. Label it C."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.121,
            0.618,
            0.47,
            0.67
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4. Are the particles visible in each mixture? "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Record",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " your observations."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.12,
            0.672,
            0.47,
            0.791
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5. Direct the light from a laser pointer through the beakers containing the mixtures (Fig. 5.3) and "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "observe",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " it from the side of the beaker in a direction perpendicular to the laser beam. Record your observations."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.108,
            0.793,
            0.469,
            0.842
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Safety first",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ": Do not look directly into the laser beam. It can cause irreversible eye damage."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.121,
            0.844,
            0.469,
            0.912
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "6. "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Predict",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " what you would observe in each of the beakers if you leave them undisturbed for a few minutes."
            }
          ]
        },
